# Archestimator - Cursor Rules (Legacy .cursorrules for back-compat)

> Full SOTA rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. This file is a concise entry point.

## Project

**Archestimator** - construction cost estimating platform (AEC, Philippines + SE Asia).
Mission: "From cost proposal to client approval."

## Stack

Next.js 16 (App Router, RSC, Cache Components) · React 19 · Bun · TypeScript strict · Tailwind v4 (CSS-first) · OpenNext for Cloudflare Workers · D1 (`ARCH_DB`) · R2 (`ARCH_UPLOADS_R2`) · Durable Objects (`COLLAB_ROOMS`) · Queues + Cron · Cloudflare Email · Cloudflare Images · Better Auth 1.6 (Google OAuth + magic link, D1-backed) · TanStack Query/Table/Virtual · Zustand · D3 · React Complex Tree · Radix · ExcelJS · Phosphor/Lucide · Vitest + Bun test + Playwright.

**Historical only (do not mutate/extend):** Supabase (`./supabase/migrations/`, project `ebxxqidacheyapmmzavr`), Resend, Vercel.

## Authority Hierarchy

1. User intent (current explicit request) - product goal
2. Repo reality (`AGENTS.md`, `.ai/`, source, tests, migrations, `wrangler.jsonc`) - implementation truth
3. Installed framework docs (`node_modules/next/dist/docs/`, Cloudflare docs) - version behavior
4. Older plans + model memory - low authority

## Read First

- `AGENTS.md` (repo root) - entry point
- `.ai/10_state/current-state.md` - FAST PATH block at top only, then `rg` for task area
- Pull `.ai/00_system/*`, `.ai/06_specs/*`, `DESIGN.md` on demand

## Shared-Worktree Safety (Non-Negotiable)

Multiple agents + humans share this worktree. NEVER auto-create/switch/delete branches, NEVER auto-push, NEVER create worktrees, NEVER `git reset --hard` / `git clean` / force-push without explicit request. Stay on current checkout. Use file-scope ownership + fresh `git status` checks + small diffs.

Re-read files immediately before editing. Preserve unfamiliar changes - they may be another agent's in-progress work. Roll back only your own edits.

## Validation (No 'Done' Without Proof) — User Test Authorization Gate

**Tests are user-gated, not automatic.** Do not create, expand, repair, or run
any automated test, test suite, build-as-test-gate, browser automation, or
broad validation gate unless Philip has explicitly requested testing for the
current task. This is the supreme rule and overrides every `TARGETED`,
`MVP-critical`, blast-radius, or "nearby tests exist" consideration. When tests
seem warranted (e.g. a critical risk cheaper evidence cannot prove), record a
`TEST_PROPOSAL` (named risk + exact command) and wait — do not run them.
`TEST_TASK` is the only execution trigger and requires an explicit user request.

Default non-test verification (encouraged without authorization):

```bash
bun run type-check         # tsc --noEmit
bun run lint               # ESLint
bun run ops:agent-debug-snapshot   # read-only debugging readiness
bun run logs:debug                  # latest dev error
git diff --check                   # whitespace/conflict audit
```

User-authorized test/build surfaces (run ONLY when Philip explicitly asks):

```bash
bun run test               # Bun unit
bun run test:dom           # Vitest DOM
bun run validate           # broad gate: type + lint + error-handling + design + unit + dom
bun run build              # Next.js production build
```

Evidence classes (strongest that proves the claim): local static -> local automated -> browser/manual -> provider-backed -> hosted/production. Inferred reasoning is not proof.

## Forbidden

- `as any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error` type suppressions
- Empty `catch (e) {}` in server/API/observability/email/ops surfaces
- `console.error` bypassing structured logger in covered runtime paths
- Deleting failing tests to make build green
- Type assertions to satisfy broken types - fix the types
- Drive-by refactors / formatting churn unrelated to the task
- Creating or running tests without explicit user authorization, even for
  auth/db/security/release/route-wide changes (propose via `TEST_PROPOSAL` and
  wait instead)

## Stack Discipline

- **Server Components by default.** Justify every `"use client"` boundary. Keep server-only data out of client bundles.
- **Server Actions are POST endpoints.** Validate auth + authz + ownership + input + idempotency on every one.
- **D1 has no RLS.** App-layer authorization enforced in repositories, Server Actions, and Better Auth route gate (`src/lib/auth/request-proxy.ts` via `src/middleware.ts`). Fail-closed by default.
- **Cache Components (Next.js 16+):** Identify static/dynamic/partial routes, name `use cache` boundaries, prove token-bearing/auth/share/upload/AI/security responses default to no-store. Don't carry over Next 14/15 cache assumptions - read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` first.
- **Repository boundary:** All D1 access through `src/lib/repositories/` helpers. No raw D1 calls from Server Actions or route handlers.
- **Optimistic mutations:** TanStack Query for server state (30s staleTime, optimistic rollbacks). Zustand for high-frequency UI state (selections, expansions).
- **Realtime:** Cloudflare Durable Objects broadcast cursors/presence via WebSocket.
- **Design system:** SF Pro, 12px max font in-app, xs-only radius (3px), zero letter-spacing, neutral palette. Reuse `src/components/ui/` primitives first.

## Cloudflare Resource Boundary

Stay inside `wrangler.jsonc` bindings: Worker `archestimator-proof`, D1 `ARCH_DB`, R2 `ARCH_UPLOADS_R2`, DO `COLLAB_ROOMS`, Queue `UPLOAD_JOBS_QUEUE`, Email `EMAIL`, Images `IMAGES`. Standing authorization covers D1/R2/DO/Queue/Email/Images mutations in these bindings. Never mutate the historical Supabase project, the unrelated `archestimator` provider project, or other Cloudflare accounts.

## Multi-Agent Execution Directive

For non-trivial work, follow `.ai/08_prompts/000_Planning Prompts/Multi-Agent-Execution-Directive.md`:
DISCOVER -> PLAN -> EXECUTE -> VERIFY -> RECORD -> REVIEW -> DECIDE, looped until gates pass or a true blocker remains. Maker/checker separation when practical. Adversarial QA for runtime/data/auth/security surfaces.

